1
00:00:00,047 --> 00:00:00,920
One person on the bus

2
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:01,810
yawns...

3
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:02,970
then the next...

4
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:03,910
then the next...

5
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:05,008
and then...

6
00:00:05,008 --> 00:00:06,700
yoooou.

7
00:00:07,328 --> 00:00:08,333
Thanks, stranger.

8
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,200
That's contagious yawning.

9
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,098
About half of adults

10
00:00:11,098 --> 00:00:11,767
catch it.

11
00:00:12,558 --> 00:00:13,070
Why?

12
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:13,940
Honestly...

13
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:15,033
nobody's sure.

14
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,010
One idea:

15
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:17,678
yawns cool your brain.

16
00:00:17,678 --> 00:00:19,360
A big gulp of air...

17
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,398
a rush of fresh blood.

18
00:00:21,761 --> 00:00:22,610
People with a cold pack

19
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:23,395
on their forehead

20
00:00:23,395 --> 00:00:26,200
caught WAY fewer yawns.

21
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:27,170
Another idea:

22
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,115
it's social.

23
00:00:28,115 --> 00:00:29,079
We copy the faces

24
00:00:29,079 --> 00:00:30,200
around us...

25
00:00:30,249 --> 00:00:31,810
some dogs even catch

26
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:33,000
OURS.

27
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,500
And the weirdest part?

28
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,419
Just READING about yawns...

29
00:00:37,419 --> 00:00:38,700
can start one.

30
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:39,652
So if you yawned

31
00:00:39,652 --> 00:00:40,920
during this...

32
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,315
it's not boredom.

33
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,600
It's science.

34
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:44,498
Tomorrow:

35
00:00:44,498 --> 00:00:46,800
why your stomach growls.

36
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,840
Subscribe...

37
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,588
if you're still awake.

